# One row a section of test-tatty.sh, in the order it has there (bash tools/test-tatty.sh --list).
# slug, extra needs, seconds. A section already needs the nearest earlier section that defines a shell variable or
# function it uses (test-tatty-plan.py reads the script for that); the extra needs are the ones from state instead: a
# feature or board an earlier section made, a file it wrote. Seconds are about what the section takes alone, to balance
# the groups of a parallel run; time one with TATTY_TIMES=<file> (test-tatty.sh writes when each section began).
